  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}=250,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{y}_{i}=265, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}^{2}=3\\,460,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{y}_{i}^{2}=5\\,720.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =3\\,460-\\frac{1}{25}(250)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\,460-2\\,500 \\\\  & =960.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
